    "title": "Artemis II mission to send crew around the moon. Everything to know",
    "text": "SPACEArtemis II mission to make history after Florida launch. What to knowHere's everything you need to know before four astronauts launch from Florida's Kennedy Space Center on a defining journey around the moon. Eric LagattaUSA TODAY NETWORK - FloridaMarch 30, 2026Updated March 31, 2026, 6:10 a.m. ETIn a matter of days, three Americans and one Canadian will set their sights on heading toward the moon for the first time in more than half-a-century.Yes, robotic U.S. landers have begun to touch down on the moon in recent years. But ever since the Apollo era came to an end in 1972, humans have yet to venture back anywhere near Earth's celestial neighbor.",
